<problem><title>Video review questions</title>
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>A general solution to the continuous linear dynamical system given by
  <me>\frac{dx}{dt} = r x</me>
where <m>r</m> is the growth or decay rate of the population, is
  <answer name="ans1a">
    <choice><m>x(t) = r \frac{x^2}{2} + C</m></choice>
    <choice><m>x(t) = r + C</m></choice>
    <choice credit="1"><m>x(t) = Ce^{rt}</m></choice>
  </answer></p>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>A solution which takes into account the initial condition <m>x(0) = x_0</m> is given by
  <me>x(t) = x_0 e^{rt}.</me></p>
<p>This is known as the
  <answer name="ans1b">
    <choice credit="1">specific solution</choice>
    <choice>initial solution</choice>
    <choice>equilibrium solution</choice>
  </answer></p>
</exercise>
</problem>
</section>


